**[PATTERN]:** Defining a fixed concurrency window for "concurrent" events (e.g., emergency triggers) supports modeling real-world bounded simultaneity.

**[EVENT]:** Added explicit fact enforcing injectivity of `timeValue` to guarantee distinct timestamps for distinct Time atoms, ensuring correct temporal comparisons.

**[EVENT]:** Replaced all temporal arithmetic and ordering constraints to use integer arithmetic on `timeValue`, including mode transitions, request processing order, delegation expiry, and credential update timing.

**[LESSON]:** Abstract flags representing credential update events simplify modeling of required post-emergency actions without overcomplicating state transitions.

**[PATTERN]:** Incremental predicates (R1, R1R2, etc.) facilitate stepwise verification of composite temporal and behavioral requirements.

**[EVENT]:** Introduced parameterized concurrency window and emergency duration constants as integer functions for flexible adjustment and clarity.

**[LESSON]:** Maintaining mutual exclusivity constraints conditional on system mode captures suspension during Emergency mode, preserving original system safety assumptions in Normal mode.

