- Parameterizing temporal constants like concurrency window and Emergency duration supports flexible, maintainable models.  
- Embedding vacuity checks ensures predicates represent meaningful scenarios, preventing false positives.  
- Explicitly defining subsets or criteria for conditional constraints (mutual exclusivity suspension, emergency privileges) clarifies requirements and supports verification.  
- Modeling credential updates as explicit Boolean flags tied temporally to Emergency termination eases verification of post-event obligations.

**[PATTERN]:**  
- `util/ordering[Time]` combined with total injective `timeValue` function is a robust Alloy pattern for discrete time handling.  
- Incremental verification of combined requirements (R1, R1R2, R1R2R3, etc.) helps localize and resolve inconsistencies.  
- Vacuity detection embedded in predicates prevents trivial satisfactions and increases verification trustworthiness.  
- Explicit symmetry and distinctness constraints on mutual exclusivity relations prevent modeling errors.  
