- Incremental verification of combined requirement predicates (R1, R1R2, R1R2R3, R1R2R3R4) helps localize and resolve inconsistencies.  
- Vacuity detection embedded in predicates prevents trivial satisfactions and increases verification trustworthiness.  
- Explicit symmetry and distinctness constraints on mutual exclusivity relations prevent modeling errors and enforce correctness.  
- Parameterized constants and event flags effectively capture dynamic temporal properties and system state changes.  

